### Modes

Every source records a mode: `.seqFlow`, `Flows#`, `Map.elems` and the merges (so also `Map.flow(f)`) record `Seq` and `.hintSequential`; `.flow` with no argument, `Range.flow(stepSize)` and `Map.keys` record `ParImm`; `.flow(mode)` records the mode passed. The mode changes nothing a flow expression returns: it selects which misuse errors of **Misuse errors** apply, and which strategies the terminal may pick (**Sources and modes**).

### Core methods

The core methods have a direct implementation, given here as pseudocode.
`for(E e: in)` receives the elements the stage before sends downstream, in flow order, one at a time: the stages before run on the element at flow order `j+1` only after the body has finished with the element at flow order `j`. `in.list` receives every element into a fresh list first. `out` is the sink of the stage, an `ActorSink` of **Signatures**: `out.send(x)` is `out#x`. `stop` ends the receiving: no stage before runs on any other element.

**`fold(acc, f)`**:
```
R r= acc#;
for(E e: in){ r= f#(r, e); }
return r;
```
**`forEach(a, f)`**:
```
for(E e: in){ f#(a, e); }
return Void;
```
**`actorMut(state, f)`** and **`actor(state, f)`**:
```
S s= state;
for(E e: in){ if(f#(out, s, e) == Break#){ stop; } }
```

**`allToAll(f)`**:
```
List[E] xs= in.list;
for(R r: f#xs){ out.send(r); }
```
**`distinct(by)`**, core since no `actor` can keep a `read` key and send `read` elements:
```
Var[List[_HashedKey[K]]] keys= {};
for(E e: in){ if(_KeepNew#(keys, by#e)){ out.send(e); } }
```
**`suppressMisuseExceptions`** is recorded in the chain, where `checkMisuse` reads it:
```
for(E e: in){ out.send(e); }
```

**`hintSequential`** and **`hintParallel`** record a hint in the chain:
```
for(E e: in){ out.send(e); }
```

**`recoverFlow`** records a mode in the chain:
```
for(E e: in){ out.send(e); }
```
The part it starts has the mode passed, and holds only the hints written after the `.recoverFlow`.

**sources**:
```
for(E e: <the elements of the receiver, in its order>){ out.send(e); }
```

**multi flow methods**: a multi flow holds its channels `c1, .., cn` as lists. `Map.flow` makes a `BiFlow` whose channels are the keys and the elements of the map, in insertion order.
`tryGetMerge(f)` returns an `Action` holding an `Info` with the sizes of the channels when the channels differ in size, before any call of `f`; otherwise it returns `.ok` of the flow whose source is:
```
for(Nat i: 0 ..< c1.size){ out.send(f#(c1.get i, .., cn.get i)); }
```
`mergeOpts(f)` runs over the indexes of the longest channel, handing `f` `.some` of the element of each channel at that index, or `.empty` past the end of that channel.
`tryGetFold`, `foldOpts`, `tryGetFoldUntil` and `foldOptsUntil` run the same loops as `fold` does, and the `Until` forms stop as soon as `pred` returns `True` for the accumulator, checked before each index.

**Lazy:** The user provided lambdas are not run until the terminal is called.

**Consumed:** A flow is consumed by the call that adds the next stage or the terminal: calling a stage or a terminal on a flow that is already consumed throws a deterministic error.

### From the desugarings to the misuse errors

The signatures and the core methods above are the whole semantics of `Base:Defensive` (see `BaseOffensiveDefensiveNaive`): a desugared method runs its desugaring when it is called, and no misuse error is ever thrown.

The misuse errors of `Base:Offensive` are decided on the chain as the user wrote it, such as `.map f .limit n`, not on the core methods it desugars to, such as two `actorMut`.

### Misuse errors

A misuse error is a non deterministic error the terminal throws to report a likely mistake in the whole flow expression.
`checkMisuse` decides from the chain, the elements of the source and the onlyImmCapture flag of each lambda; `checkMisuse` never runs a lambda.

Every terminal starts with `checkMisuse(c)`, where `c` is its chain:
- `c.mode` (the mode the source records), `c.source` (the elements of the source), `c.stages` (in order, indexed from `0`), `c.terminal`;
- `c.parts`: the parts of the chain; `p.hints` are the hints of the part `p`; a hint is not in `c.stages`;
- `c.lambdas`: every lambda of the chain; `l.owner` is the stage/terminal `l` is an argument of;
- `l.onlyImmCapture`: `l` captures only `imm` values; a top level declaration used as a value and every `imm` lambda carry it.

A shape pattern matches a contiguous part of the source, the stages and the terminal: `..` is any sequence, possibly empty, `X*` any sequence of stages in the set `X`, `X+` a non empty one, `s[i]` the stage at index `i`, `source` the source. In an error text, `<s>` of a stage/terminal `s` is `show(s)`, `<X>` of a sequence `X` of stages/terminals is the `show` of each, joined with a space, and `<a>` of an argument `a` is `showArg(a)`:
```
Str show(Step s)= s.name + match s.args{
  [] -> "";
  [a] with showArg(a) == "{..}" -> "{..}";
  [a] -> " " + showArg(a);
  as -> "(" + as.map(showArg).join(", ") + ")"
  }
Str showArg(Object a)= match a{
  Nat|Byte|Int|Num|Float n -> n.str;
  Str t with t.size <= 20 -> "\"" + t + "\"";
  Str t -> "\"" + t.subString(0, 20) + "..\"";
  _ -> "{..}"
  }
```
So `.sort by .filter p .size` shows as `.sort{..} .filter{..} .size`, `.limit 5 .limit 3` as `.limit 5 .limit 3`, and `.join ", "` as `.join ", "`.
```
Fence=        {allToAll, sort, sortDistinct, max, min, distinctMut, ++}
OneToOne=     {map, peek, scan, readOnly, map(ctx, _), peek(ctx, _), recoverFlow}
ElemLambda=   OneToOne + {filter, flatMap, flatMapMut, mapFilter, actor, actorMut}
ToRead=       {++, flatMap, distinct, actor, scan, readOnly}
Decision=     {limit, actor, actorMut}
ShortCircuit= {first, findFirst, findMap, any, all, none}
mutReach(i)=  c.stages.subList(0, i).none(ToRead + {recoverFlow(ParImm), recoverFlow(ParRead)})

Void checkMisuse(Chain c){
  if(c.stages.contains(suppressMisuseExceptions)){ return; }
  if(c.mode in {ParRepr, ParPod}){ checkPar(c); }
  if(c.mode == Seq && c.stages.contains(recoverFlow)){ checkDecisions(c); }
  checkForEach(c);
  checkShape(c);
  }
Void checkPar(Chain c){
  if(exists i != j: c.source.get(i) == c.source.get(j)){ throw
    "The elements at index <i> and <j> of the source are identity equal: each element of a `<c.mode>` flow must be a distinct object."; }
  for(Lambda l: c.lambdas){
    if(!l.onlyImmCapture && l.owner not in {for, forEach}){ throw
      "The lambda of `<l.owner>` captures a value that is not `imm`: over `ParRepr` and `ParPod` only the lambdas of `.for` and `.forEach` may capture `read` or `mut` values."; }
    }
  checkDecisions(c);
  }
Void checkDecisions(Chain c){
  match c.shape{
    .. s[i] X* d ..
      with s in ElemLambda, mutReach(i), X.none(Fence), d in Decision + ShortCircuit,
      !(d in {limit, first} && (s X).all(OneToOne))
      -> throw decisionMsg(s, d);
    .. d[i] with d in ShortCircuit - {first}, mutReach(i) -> throw decisionMsg(d, d);
    _ -> {}
    }
  }
Str decisionMsg(Stage s, Stage d)=
  "`<s>` is a speculating stage of the speculation driver `<d>` and receives its elements as `mut`: it can not run in parallel without mutating elements the flow may never process. End the flow expression with `.list` before `<d>`, and continue with `.seqFlow`."
Void checkForEach(Chain c){
  match c.shape{
    .. f X+ .forEach with f in Fence + {source}, X.none(Fence) ->
      Bool seqOk= c.mode == Seq && X.none(ToRead);
      Bool immOk= c.mode == ParImm
        && c.lambdas.filter{l -> l.owner != forEach}.all{l -> l.onlyImmCapture}
        && c.stages.none({flatMapMut, actorMut, allToAll, ++});
      if(!seqOk && !immOk){ throw
        "`.forEach` runs its lambda while `<X>` may still run on the elements after, preventing the parallelism `<c.mode>` asks for: write `.for`, which runs its lambda once every stage has finished."; }
    _ -> {}
    }
  }
```
Deceptive shape errors:
```
CountChanging= {filter, flatMap, flatMapMut, mapFilter}
ReadsEmpty=  {map, readOnly, ++, scan, sort, distinct, distinctMut, sortDistinct, max, min, limit}* .isEmpty
ReadsCount=  {map, readOnly, ++, scan, sort, limit}* .size
ReadsElems=  ({map, readOnly, ++, sort, max, min} + CountChanging)* (
               {get, getOpt, sum(sn)} with sn the SumNumber of Nat, Byte or Num
             | (CountChanging + {distinct, distinctMut, sortDistinct, max, min}) ReadsCount
             | CountChanging ReadsEmpty )
ReadsFirst=  {map, readOnly, ++, scan, distinct, distinctMut, limit}* .first
```
```
Void checkShape(Chain c){
  for(Part p: c.parts){ if(p.hints.size > 1){ throw
    "A flow takes at most one of `.hintSequential` and `.hintParallel` in each part between `.recoverFlow` calls, but this part has "+p.hints.size+". A flow started with `.seqFlow`, `Flows#`, `Map.elems` or a merge of a `BiFlow`, `TriFlow` or `QuadFlow` already has `.hintSequential`. Keep only one."; } }
  match c.shape{
    .. s rest with s in {sort}, rest in ReadsEmpty | ReadsCount | ReadsElems
    .. s rest with s in {map, scan}, rest in ReadsEmpty | ReadsCount
    .. s rest with s in {distinct, distinctMut}, rest in ReadsEmpty | ReadsFirst
    .. s rest with s in {sortDistinct, max, min}, rest in ReadsEmpty
      -> throw "`<s>` is pointless: `<rest>` reads only "+match rest{
        ReadsEmpty -> "whether there are elements";
        ReadsCount -> "how many elements there are";
        ReadsElems -> "which elements there are, in any order";
        ReadsFirst -> "the first element" }+", and `<s>` does not change that. Remove `<s>`.";
    .. .sort by1 .sort by2 .. -> throw
      "Two sorting stages in a row: `.sort <by1> .sort <by2>` is one sort by `<by2>` with ties ordered by `<by1>`. Write `.sort(<by2>.then <by1>)`, or `.sort(<by1>.then <by2>)` if `<by1>` is the main order.";
    .. .limit n .limit m .. -> throw
      "Two limits in a row: `.limit <n> .limit <m>` keeps the first <n.min(m)> elements. Write `.limit <n.min(m)>`.";
    .. X+ .limit n .. with X.all(OneToOne) -> throw
      "`<X> .limit <n>` runs `<X>` on the same elements as `.limit <n> <X>`. Write `.limit <n> <X>`.";
    .. f .forEach with f in Fence + {source} -> throw
      "`.forEach` directly after `<f>` has no stage to run while it receives the elements. Write `.for`.";
    .. m {sort, max, min, sortDistinct, distinctMut, limit}* t ..
      with m in {flatMapMut f, distinctMut by}, t in {distinct, ++, size, isEmpty} -> throw
      "`<m>` sends `mut` elements downstream, but `<t>` discards their mutability. Write "+match m{
        flatMapMut f -> "`.flatMap <f>`";
        distinctMut by -> "`.distinct <by>`" }+".";
    .. .sort by1 s .. with s in {max by2, min by2} -> throw
      "Wasted sorting: `.sort <by1> <s>` sorts the elements `<s>` drops. Write `<s> .sort <by1>`.";
    .. s t with s in {sort by, sortDistinct by}, t in {first, last} -> throw
